## 8. Documentation & Changesets

### README Update
**File**: `renderers/tinymce/README.md` (new section)

```markdown
## Formats Plugin: Pantoken Classes on Built-in Commands

The opt-in `createFormatsPlugin` adds `instui-*` classes to TinyMCE's native format commands 
(bold, italic, underline, headings, links, lists, tables, images) so generated content 
integrates seamlessly with pantoken's CSS without requiring custom dialogs or pickers.

### Usage

```ts
import { createFormatsPlugin } from '@pantoken/tinymce';

tinymce.PluginManager.add('pantoken_formats', createFormatsPlugin({
  prefix: 'instui',  // Default
  formats: {
    bold: { classes: ['my-bold'] },  // Override
  },
  onApply: (element, formatName) => console.log(`Applied ${formatName}`),
}));
```

### Default Classes

| Format | Class | Notes |
|--------|-------|-------|
| bold | `.instui-bold` | Applied to `<strong>` |
| italic | `.instui-italic` | Applied to `<em>` |
| heading (h2–h6) | `.instui-h2`, etc. | Applied to block element |
| link | `.instui-link` | Applied to `<a>` |
| list | `.instui-list-item` | Applied to `<li>` |
| table | `.instui-table` | Applied to `<table>`; cells/rows also get `.instui-table-cell`, etc. |

### Canvas RCE Note

Canvas's server-side HTML sanitizer preserves `class`, `id`, `style`, and `role` attributes 
on all elements. Pantoken's `instui-*` classes survive the save–roundtrip intact.
```

